   "answer": "BERT randomly chooses 15% of the WordPiece tokens in each sequence for prediction [c_1]. Each chosen token is replaced as follows:\n\n- **80% of the time:** it is replaced with the [MASK] token.\n- **10% of the time:** it is replaced with a random token.\n- **10% of the time:** it is left unchanged [c_1].\n\nThe model then uses the final hidden vector Ti to predict the original token with cross-entropy loss [c_1].\n\nThe mixed replacement reduces the mismatch between pre-training and fine-tuning, because [MASK] never appears during fine-tuning [c_1][c_3]. Keeping some tokens unchanged biases the representation toward the actual observed word [c_2]. Random replacement affects only 1.5% of all tokens (10% of 15%), which does not seem to harm language understanding [c_2].",
