   },
   "answer": "The index hot-swapping experiment showed that RAG's accuracy drops sharply when the index doesn't match the time period of the question [c_1].\n\n- **Matched indices:** RAG answered 70% correctly using the 2016 index for 2016 world leaders, and 68% using the 2018 index for 2018 world leaders [c_1].\n- **Mismatched indices:** Accuracy was low, at 12% with the 2018 index and 2016 leaders, and 4% with the 2016 index and 2018 leaders [c_1].\n\nThe setup used 82 world leaders who changed between the two dates. The 2016 index was the DrQA Wikipedia dump from December 2016, and the 2018 index was the December 2018 dump. Each was queried with the template \"Who is {position}?\" using the NQ RAG model [c_1].\n\nThe authors concluded that RAG's world knowledge can be updated by simply replacing its non-parametric memory [c_1].",
