   },
   "answer": "The authors observe a distinctive U-shaped performance curve. Models perform best when the relevant information is at the very beginning (primacy bias) or the very end (recency bias) of the input context. Performance drops significantly when the information is in the middle [c_1][c_2][c_6].\n\nSome details:\n- GPT-3.5-Turbo's multi-document QA performance can fall by more than 20% depending on position. In the worst case, in the 20- and 30-document settings, it is lower than the closed-book result of 56.1% [c_6].\n- The U-shape also appears in the synthetic key-value retrieval task for some models [c_4].\n- Encoder-decoder models are relatively robust within their training-time sequence length, but show the U-shape on longer sequences [c_3][c_4].\n- Base models without instruction fine-tuning also show the U-shape [c_4][c_5].\n- In Llama-2, the 7B models are solely recency biased, while the 13B and 70B models show the U-shape [c_5].",
